Z||000000||BOSTITCH||08-09-2000||07:48 PM||||I did the 3.1 conv. and a centerforce clutch. I let it break in and everything but it slips at peak torque 4200 rpms or so. I bought the clucth for a 4cyl. 5spd 86' everything fit good used the same slave the flywheel was machined. If anyone has any suggestions it would be helpful  e-mail me also thanx.<BR> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||08-09-2000||08:58 PM||||If you used the clutch for the Isuzu tranny, everything should be fine. I wonder if the clutch is bad or contaminated with oil or something. I have the Isuzu in my Fiero with the V6 with no problems. I did have a problem when I first did the swap though - I used the TO bearing from the Isuzu and the plate from the V6 which was mated to a 4 speed. I ended up dropping the cradle to replace the clutch with one for the Isuzu. I used everything for the Isuzu and nothing from the 4 speed.<P>Did you use all the components for the Isuzu?||||reg||1
